{"role":"assistant","content":"Fixed the nightly job and documented everything in `ANSWER.md`.\n\nCauses:\n- Missing `USER` in launchd’s environment caused Claude’s repeated “Not logged in” errors.\n- Assigning to zsh’s read-only `status` variable terminated the wrapper before either success or failure notification.\n- The agent invocation also left stdin open, creating a potential launchd hang.\n\nChanges:\n- Added `USER=vk` to `Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist`.\n- Renamed `status` to `rc` and added `< /dev/null` in `bin/nightly-review.zsh`.\n\nValidation passed: plist/script syntax checks, successful output and notification path, forced-failure notification with exit code preserved, and immediate stdin EOF. Tests used local stand-ins; nothing was deployed or sent externally."}
